            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Competitive Analysis and Market Positioning</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Understanding the competitive landscape is essential for creating a
                    differentiated product position. Competitive analysis helps teams
                    identify gaps in the market, understand customer alternatives, and
                    determine where the product can create stronger value.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Competitor Analysis</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Evaluate competitor products, pricing, features, customer experience,
                    positioning, strengths, and weaknesses to understand how the market
                    currently serves customer needs.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Alternative Solutions</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Customers may solve their problems using internal processes,
                    traditional methods, or other technologies instead of direct
                    competitors. Understanding these alternatives creates a broader view
                    of the competitive environment.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Market Gaps</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Identify customer requirements that are not being adequately addressed
                    by existing products. These gaps can provide opportunities for stronger
                    product differentiation.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Positioning Opportunities</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Use competitive and customer insights to determine the market space
                    where the product can provide meaningful and defensible value.
                </p>
            </div>

